# The build context BuildKit uploads before any COPY runs. Without this file the context
# is the whole working tree: .venv, .git, docs/ and notebooks/ come to roughly 3.5 GB
# locally and 1.3 GB on a fresh CI checkout, and no layer in the Dockerfile reads any of
# it.
#
# The Dockerfile copies four paths and nothing else, so this excludes everything and
# re-includes exactly those. A COPY added later without a matching entry here fails the
# build outright rather than quietly shipping whatever happened to be on disk. Excluding
# .git is deliberate and already assumed: the Dockerfile takes the version through the
# SRM_VERSION build arg precisely because git metadata is not copied in.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src
!configs

# COPY src/ ./src/ takes the tree as it is on disk, so local build artifacts ship in the
# image and change that layer's hash after any local test run. The bytecode is the worst
# of it, since a developer machine leaves cpython-314 .pyc files in a tree the runtime
# reads with Python 3.13, and UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE regenerates what is actually needed.
src/**/__pycache__
src/**/*.py[cod]
src/**/.ipynb_checkpoints
src/*.egg-info
